# Local development environment for awesome-agent-trust maintenance.
# Copy this file to .env (or export the variables directly) when running
# the maintenance scripts in .github/scripts/ locally.
#
# Tokens are only used to raise the GitHub API rate limit
# (60 requests/hour unauthenticated vs 5,000 requests/hour authenticated).
# List submissions never require a token.

# Preferred: run `gh auth login` once and leave both variables below empty.
# The scripts then fall back to the GitHub CLI credential, so nothing has to
# be scoped, expiring, or stored in this file.
#
# Set these only when you cannot use the GitHub CLI. GH_TOKEN wins over
# GITHUB_TOKEN, and either one wins over the `gh auth login` session: a stale
# exported value fails with HTTP 401 instead of falling back, so run
# `unset GH_TOKEN GITHUB_TOKEN` if `gh` itself starts returning 401.
#
# A personal access token needs no scopes for public repository metadata; the
# `repo` scope is NOT required. CI sets GH_TOKEN itself.
GH_TOKEN=
GITHUB_TOKEN=